    "updated_at": "2023-06-26T19:41:08Z",
    "body": "> This patch also makes removal of the popover attribute stop firing events in order to signal to the hide popover algorithm that checks for the popover attribute should be ignored.\r\n\r\nIf anyone thinks that we should continue firing events when script runs `element.removeAttribute('popover')` on a showing popover, then I could modify this PR to do so by adding additional plumbing of flags around the algorithms. Does anyone have opinions on this?",
