    "body": "> If anyone thinks that we should continue firing events when script runs `element.removeAttribute('popover')` on a showing popover\r\n\r\nIt would increase inconsistency of the Popover API's behavior. Including making the (non-normative) description of the \"beforetoggle\" event (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-beforetoggle) less precise.",
