    "created_at": "2023-09-04T11:23:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-04T11:23:18Z",
    "body": "> It would be helpful to have use-cases for the \"beforetoggle\" event in case a popover is hidden.\r\nIf there are some, they should be supported. Otherwise, it would presumably allow simplifying the spec, and implementations, significantly. No \"ignoreDomState\" might be required and nested hiding might also not be possible anymore. It might also simplify augmenting the popover feature for popover=hint, which presumably will happen during this year.\r\n\r\n@mfreed7 do you have any opinions about removing beforetoggle events during attribute removal or node removal?",
